---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const breadcrumbItems = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Terms' },
];

const lastUpdated = '24 May 2026';
export const prerender = true;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use · Peninsula Insider"
  description="Terms of use for Peninsula Insider - editorial guidance, recommendations, accounts, Ask PI, and acceptable use."
  section="home"
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbItems} />

  <section class="legal">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="legal__header">
        <p class="label label--accent">Terms</p>
        <h1 class="legal__title">Terms of Use</h1>
        <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal__body prose">
        <p>Peninsula Insider is an independent editorial publication about the Mornington Peninsula. By accessing or using this site, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the site.</p>

        <h2>What Peninsula Insider is</h2>
        <p>Peninsula Insider provides editorially curated recommendations, planning guidance, and destination information about the Mornington Peninsula. Our content is designed to help you discover and plan Peninsula experiences - it is editorial guidance, not a booking service or a guarantee of any particular experience.</p>

        <h2>Recommendations and editorial guidance</h2>
        <p>Recommendations on Peninsula Insider reflect editorial judgement based on research, local knowledge, and ongoing coverage of the Peninsula. They are genuine - not paid placements or commercially influenced listings (see <a href="/editorial-approach/">Editorial Approach</a> for how coverage decisions are made).</p>
        <p>Recommendations describe what we observed and what we think makes a place worth your time. They are not guarantees. We recommend places because we believe in them, but:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>venue experiences can vary by season, staffing, and conditions</li>
          <li>opening hours, menus, and pricing change</li>
          <li>bookings sell out and events move</li>
          <li>venues occasionally close or change significantly</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Before committing to a booking or making a special trip, we encourage you to confirm key details directly with the venue or operator.</p>

        <h2>Ask PI</h2>
        <p>Ask PI provides planning guidance and recommendations drawn from Peninsula Insider's editorial knowledge of the region. Ask PI responses are based on our best available information but should be treated as a starting point for planning, not a definitive or real-time source.</p>
        <p>Ask PI does not have live access to booking availability, current opening hours, or real-time event status. Conditions, prices, and availability can change between when our content was written and when you visit. For anything time-sensitive - a booking, a special occasion, a long drive - please confirm the details directly with the venue or operator before you go.</p>
        <p>Ask PI recommendations reflect Peninsula Insider's editorial perspective and are independent of commercial relationships. A recommendation from Ask PI means we think it's genuinely worth considering - it does not mean the venue is aware of, or has endorsed, the suggestion.</p>

        <h2>Saved places and plans</h2>
        <p>Saving places and building plans on Peninsula Insider is a personal planning tool. Saved content reflects information at the time it was saved - we don't update your saved lists when venue details change. Check the current venue page or contact the operator before acting on a saved recommendation, especially if some time has passed since you saved it.</p>
        <p>Accounts and saved content are personal to you. You are responsible for maintaining the security of your sign-in credentials. To delete your account or saved data, see <a href="/privacy/">our privacy policy</a> or contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@peninsulainsider.com.au">hello@peninsulainsider.com.au</a>.</p>

        <h2>Accuracy and currency</h2>
        <p>We work to keep Peninsula Insider current and accurate. We run regular accuracy checks and act on corrections promptly. But no editorial publication can guarantee every detail is right at every moment - venues change, events shift, and conditions vary. If you spot something that looks wrong, we genuinely want to know: <a href="mailto:corrections@peninsulainsider.com.au">corrections@peninsulainsider.com.au</a>.</p>

        <h2>Partnerships and editorial independence</h2>
        <p>Peninsula Insider may work with Peninsula venues and operators through editorial partnerships. Where this occurs, it does not influence editorial recommendations - a venue is recommended because we believe it's worth your time, not because of a commercial relationship. Our <a href="/editorial-approach/">Editorial Approach</a> page explains how we handle these relationships and how coverage decisions are made.</p>
        <p>Some pages may include affiliate or referral links. Where Peninsula Insider earns a commission through these links, this occurs at no additional cost to you and does not influence editorial judgement.</p>

        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>Unless otherwise stated, all editorial copy, curation logic, original graphics, site structure, compiled guides, and branding on Peninsula Insider are protected by copyright. You may read, share, and link to content for personal or non-commercial reference. You may not republish, systematically reproduce, or commercially exploit material from the site without written permission.</p>

        <h2>Automated access and extraction</h2>
        <p>You may not use bots, scrapers, crawlers, bulk collection tools, or other automated methods to extract, reproduce, mirror, republish, or train AI models on Peninsula Insider content without express written permission. This includes building derivative destination or directory products from our editorial corpus.</p>
        <p>Reasonable search-engine indexing, citation, and linking are permitted where consistent with our robots policy and normal web use.</p>

        <h2>External links and third parties</h2>
        <p>We link to third-party venues, booking providers, and external sites. We don't control those sites and aren't responsible for their content, availability, pricing, or policies. If you book or transact with a third party, that relationship is between you and them.</p>

        <h2>No professional advice</h2>
        <p>Nothing on this site is legal, medical, financial, or safety advice. Where activities involve coastal or surf conditions, bushland, alcohol, or travel logistics, exercise your own judgement and check the relevant official guidance.</p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to use this site in a way that harms the platform or other users, interferes with site availability, misrepresents Peninsula Insider content as your own, or is unlawful or deceptive.</p>

        <h2>Future features</h2>
        <p>Peninsula Insider continues to develop new features - expanded planning tools, itineraries, recommendation layers, and community experiences. Additional terms may apply to specific features when they launch.</p>

        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms from time to time. If we make material changes, we'll update the date at the top of this page. Continued use of the site after changes take effect means you accept the revised terms.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>For permissions, licensing, or terms enquiries: <a href="mailto:hello@peninsulainsider.com.au">hello@peninsulainsider.com.au</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
